  static const String englishAgreement = """
General Terms and Conditions for the Sale of 2G/3G/4G Prepaid Offers

General Terms and Conditions for the Sale of 4G Prepaid Offers:
Preamble: This contract specifies the general terms and conditions for the sale of “Mobilis Prepaid” offers, as defined in the following paragraphs (referred to as “General Conditions (GC)”), in accordance with the applicable legislation and regulations in Algeria, especially the terms outlined in ATM Mobilis Specifications, which authorize the establishment and operation of a public network for wireless cellular communication of the types (GSM + (2G), Third Generation (3G), and Fourth Generation (4G), and the provision of services to the public.
The relationship between the parties is subject to the general terms and conditions of sale, the terms of the “Mobilis Prepaid” Package, and the pricing card applicable to the prepaid offer in which the subscriber has enrolled. The “Mobilis Prepaid” offer is financially and contractually independent from the user’s terminal.

1. Definitions:
    1.1 Customer Definitions:
        1.1.1 Subscriber: Any natural or legal person with legal capacity to undertake and be legally responsible towards ATM Mobilis, who, after pre-registration in a prepaid mobile phone subscription service, complies with the regulations under a contract identified through which he uses mobile phone services with a SIM/USIM card registered on the ATM Mobilis network.
        1.1.2 User: As per the terms of this contract (GC), a minor or a vulnerable person or an employee benefiting from a mobile phone line, granted to them by the subscriber, who is the legal guardian, the custodian or the employer. The user is not considered the holder of the subscription contract.
        1.1.3 Active Subscriber Definition: A subscriber to prepaid mobile services is considered active if, within the last one hundred and twenty (120) days, he has performed at least one of the following operations: 
        - Sent or received a voice or video call 
        - Sent a Short Message Service (SMS) or a Multimedia Messaging Service (MMS) 
        - Accessed the Internet. 

ATM Mobilis automatically suspends the subscribers’ lines that have not performed any of the mentioned operations within the specified period above. For subscribers registered in offers exceeding 120 days, the minimum deadline for suspending the operation of SIM/USIM cards corresponds to the validity period of the offer. ATM Mobilis commits to implementing mechanisms that allow subscribers to be informed before suspending the operation of their SIM/USIM cards, respecting the specified deadline mentioned above.

    1.2 Definition of the Provided Service: The provided service refers to wireless communication services of the (GSM) 2G category, Third Generation (3G), and Fourth Generation (4G), including voice, data, and multimedia services for the benefit of service users, originating from a compatible and designed mobile terminal to receive a SIM (Subscriber Identity Module) or USIM (Universal Subscriber Identity Module) card.

    1.3 Definition of SIM Card and USIM Card: USIM (Universal Subscriber Identity Module) or SIM (Subscriber Identity Module) refers to an electronic unit for subscriber identification that allows access to services.
        1.3.1 USIM/SIM Card for Recharge, Payment, and/or Activation: This refers to a USIM/SIM card exclusively used for balance recharge operations, bill payments, and/or activation of USIM/SIM cards.
        1.3.2 USIM/SIM Card Machine-to-Machine (M2M) or Internet of Things (IoT): This type of USIM/SIM card is used for communication between distant devices or things to transmit data, and incoming calls from these cards are processed without human intervention.
        1.3.3. Deactivated USIM/SIM Cards: These are USIM/SIM cards that are permanently disconnected from the operator’s network after the termination of the subscription contract.
    
    1.4 Definition of Terminal Device: The terminal device refers to a receiving device for a SIM/USIM card that enables access, through radio frequencies, to the public network of wireless communication based on standards such as GSM, GPRS, EDGE, UMTS, HSPA, HSPA+, and/or LTE-Advanced. The connection is established from all locations within the coverage area of radio stations that capture signals from the user’s device.

    1.5 Definition of 2G/3G/4G Communication Network or 2G/3G/4G Network: 
        A 2G wireless communication network refers to a public cellular communication network of the GSM type, which includes the use of technologies such as GPRS.
        A 3G wireless communication network refers to a public cellular communication network operating according to UMTS standards, allowing for a significant increase in data transfer volume.
        A 4G wireless communication network or 4G network refers to a public mobile communication network that utilizes advanced mobile wireless technologies compliant with the characteristics of International Mobile Telecommunications-Advanced (IMT- Advanced), and is used for the Long-Term Evolution (LTE Advanced) technology as defined by the International Telecommunication Union for fourth-generation (4G) wireless communication networks.

    1.6 National Roaming: National roaming refers to the ability of the subscriber to communicate by using the networks of national operators who hold licenses for (2G/3G/4G) and with whom ATM Mobilis has entered into specific agreements for national roaming, specifying the geographic areas and the pricing and billing conditions applicable. The subscriber's usage of roaming is subject to the terms of national roaming rates. The covered areas under the agreements for national roaming and the applicable roaming rates will be announced to customers. Customers will also be informed about the areas covered by the agreements for national roaming and the approved rates.

    1.7 International Roaming: International roaming allows customers to access public networks of foreign wireless cellular operators who have entered into specific agreements for roaming services with ATM Mobilis (international roaming), subject to the nature of the available services.

2. Offer Scope: Customers with the “Prepaid Mobilis” card included in the package can make and receive local and international calls and access various voice and data services within the limits of:
    (a) The amount of prepaid communication credit allocated to a refillable account, which can accumulate refill amounts and may be subject to a validity period depending on the offer.
    (b) The validity period associated with the prepaid communication credit and the threshold based on the offer.
    (c) The coverage area related to the service.

3. Pricing of Products and Services: The pricing of products and services offered by “Prepaid Mobilis”, as well as its various offers and application methods, and the cost of consumption, are subject to a pricing card prepared by ATM Mobilis for its customers. The pricing card is an integral part of the contract. ATM Mobilis reserves the right to change the offer at any time during the contract period, and it undertakes to inform the subscriber of any changes or modifications to the pricing made to an offer or plan.

4. ATM Mobilis Commitments: ATM Mobilis commits to satisfying all activation requests for the “Prepaid” offer within the limits of the systems it utilizes and the quality of services. ATM Mobilis is responsible for providing the necessary resources for the smooth operation of the “Prepaid Mobilis” offers and takes necessary measures to maintain the continuity and quality of the service. However, ATM Mobilis is not responsible for:
    • Service interruptions resulting from the obligation imposed on ATM Mobilis to cease using frequency spectrum.
    • Interruptions resulting from force majeure events or pre-authorized interruptions by the competent authorities.
    • Interruptions in telephone service for other mobile or landline networks, resulting from partial or total cessation of the operation of this operator's network for any reason.
    • Disruptions and/or partial or complete unavailability of services provided by other operators when the subscriber accesses their networks in the context of national roaming.
    • In the case of malfunction resulting from the use of terminal devices or misconfiguration of these devices or their accessories.
    • Non-compliance of the subscribers with their obligations.

ATM Mobilis is not responsible for the use of SIM and/or USIM cards or refill cards when the latter does not have a manufacturing defect. ATM Mobilis is also not responsible for the use of incompatible terminal devices with the marketed offers, considering that the expansion of the 4G network is in progress. The subscriber acknowledges that the conditions for accessing and using the services of this network may not be optimal at all times, so ATM Mobilis informs its customers about the evolving situation of the 4G network through its commercial publications or on its official website (www.mobilis.dz). ATM Mobilis does not have any contractual obligation to provide the subscriber with details of the calls they have made for the Prepaid Mobilis offer.

5. Subscriber Commitments: The subscriber commits to completing the identity verification procedures as a natural person by providing the following documents and information:
    (a) When acquiring a prepaid contract, the subscriber must present, at the point of sale, a copy of a valid and undamaged official ID card, along with presenting the original card. For minors, the contract must be signed by the legal guardian or custodian, with the necessity of attaching a document specifying the guardian’s status and a document holding them responsible for the use of the line provided by ATM Mobilis.
    (b) In the case of subscribing to the service on behalf of a user by a representative, the representative must, at the time of subscription, provide the following:
    • His valid official ID card.
    • A valid power of attorney, signed and endorsed by municipal authorities or a public notary, allowing the representative (buyer) to take the necessary steps to acquire a SIM/USIM card on his behalf.
    • The official valid ID card of the subscribing individual.
    • Copies of the above-mentioned ID cards.

It should be noted that if the formalities for identity verification are carried out at approved points of sale, and if the subscription contract along with the used documents for identity verification is not sent to ATM Mobilis within the specified deadlines or if it is not compliant or clear, ATM Mobilis reserves the right to request the subscriber to resubmit the documents to avoid service suspension.

For the legal entity, whether public or private, the following documents and information must be provided: the company’s articles of association (constitutive and amended), justifying the person authorized to sign the contract; a copy of the trade register; a proxy signed by the legally authorized person in the company allowing the person applying to contract with ATM Mobilis on behalf of and for the account of the legal entity; a copy of a valid identity card, undamaged, for the authorized person legally binding the contract, on behalf of the legal entity, along with presenting the original copy and a Certificate of Existence.

For auto-entrepreneur or self-employed individuals working in freelance professions, associations, unions, etc., the following documents and information must be provided: A copy of the trade register or accreditation certificate (for self- employment, associations, unions, etc.); a copy of the valid, undamaged national ID card, along with presenting the original copy; a copy of the professional card; Fill out and sign the prepaid payment offer contract, acknowledging and agreeing to the general and special conditions of this contract and its appendices, which are an integral part of it; Use a compatible terminal device for the service; Use the public network for wireless communications provided by ATM Mobilis in accordance with the laws and regulations in force on the date of use, as well as the recommendations of ATM Mobilis; Do not relinquish the card and phone number to a third party, except for legal relinquishment, the procedures for which are specified by ATM Mobilis; Read the special conditions for each offer, where the reference document can be downloaded from the official ATM Mobilis websites (www.mobilis.dz); Respect the conditions related to the active subscriber as stipulated in Article 1.1.3 of the general sales conditions; Provide ATM Mobilis with the subscriber's email address, if possible, to diversify communication channels with the subscriber.

6. Network Access Conditions:
    6.1 Devices Required for Accessing 2G/3G/4G Network: Accessing the 2G/3G/4G network requires the subscriber to use compatible devices and software properly configured (terminal and SIM card). The subscriber must ensure that his device can take advantage of all the benefits related to subscribing to the 2G/3G/4G service, especially the 2G/3G/4G signal.
    6.2 Access to 4G Network in Algeria: ATM Mobilis’s 4G network is expanding, and continuous coverage in certain areas may not be guaranteed or could be unstable. If the 4G network is unavailable for any reason, the subscriber will be automatically switched to the 2G/3G/GSM network of ATM Mobilis, except for services not compatible with these standards, which will be automatically suspended. Communications and interactions resulting from the automatic switch to the GSM (2G) and/or (3G) network remain subject to the pricing conditions of the subscribed offer.
    6.3 Access to International Networks: The subscriber, with the correct configuration of his terminal, can access networks of other operators with whom ATM Mobilis has signed roaming agreements, within the coverage areas of those networks. The consumption of the subscriber outside Algeria is subject to the specific pricing conditions for international roaming. The subscriber is solely responsible for his data service consumption, which can be controlled or deactivated during roaming through the terminal device or a written request to the operator.

7. Subscriber Alert:
    7.1 Alert Regarding Downloads: ATM Mobilis explicitly informs the subscriber that the contents stored, used, delivered, and received by him are his responsibility, especially when done via internet connections. Therefore, the subscriber bears full civil or criminal responsibility associated with these operations. The subscriber is also responsible for storing, downloading, or sending any prohibited, illegal, or inappropriate data that violates public decency or order. ATM Mobilis cannot be held responsible for prohibited, illegal, or unlawful content and the costs associated with calls or SMS resulting from downloading applications that generate SPAM calls and messages abroad.
    
    7.2 Subscriber Behaviour Alert and Usage Tips:
        7.2.1 Prohibited Behaviours: Subscribers are prohibited from engaging in any deceptive use of the 2G/3G/4G network, including but not limited to:
            - Deliberate or non-deliberate congestion of email service providers and ATM Mobilis networks and/or recipients of emails.
            - Using services to create voice distributors and/or redirecting paths and/or redirecting calls (voice, SMS, or MMS messages, and internet) to numbers for internet access or directed to radio mailboxes, SMS, outgoing calls for unwanted callback Msisdn (spam).
            - Sending interactive messages that necessarily generate a large number of responses, causing disruptions in the availability of distributors or the network.
            - Using SIM/USIM cards to redirect voice or SMS messages received from outside towards a Mobilis subscriber and/or another network.
            - Misusing internet access for fraudulent purposes.
            - Misusing the roaming service for fraudulent purposes, including hacking or attempting to hack activities that allow:
                - Unauthorized access to a remote control device belonging to others for controlling the device remotely.
                - Unauthorized access to an information system belonging to others for capturing all or part of the content of a website or mailbox, Transmission of viruses.

In addition, subscribers are prohibited from any commercial or collective use resulting from accessing the (2G/3G/4G) network available to them. This includes allowing others to access the ATM Mobilis network with or without payment. ATM Mobilis reserves the right to suspend, without prior notice, the SIM cards of those who commit the violations mentioned above or engage in suspicious activities identified by fraud prevention and revenue assurance systems.
        
        7.2.2 Usage Tips and Safety Conditions: when making calls or sending data, the terminal device is directly connected to radio towers, it means there is an exchange of information through electromagnetic waves. For the safety of its customers, ATM Mobilis advises taking certain measures to reduce exposure to these electromagnetic fields and vibrations:
            - Use earphones when making calls;
            - Make calls, whenever possible, in areas with high signal quality to reduce exposure to electromagnetic radiation;
            - Encourage children and teenagers to use communication devices reasonably;
            - Preferably use text messages, emails, and the internet to reduce exposure to electromagnetic radiation.

Additionally, it is necessary to respect the following safety rules:
    - For customers with implanted electronic medical devices, it is advisable to keep the terminal device at least 15 cm away from these devices and use the device on the opposite side.
    - Adhere to usage restrictions related to specific locations (hospitals, airplanes, etc.).
    - Avoid listening to loud music on the terminal device for extended periods.
    - Adhere to the usage conditions specified by the manufacturer detailed in the instructions booklet for the terminal devices.
    
    7.3 Warning Regarding the Internet: The subscriber acknowledges being fully aware of the lack of reliability of the Internet, especially concerning:
        - Absence of data transmission safety;
        - Lack of performance guarantees related to data transfer volume and speed.

It is explicitly reminded that the Internet is not a secure network, and the confidentiality of communications transmitted over the network is not guaranteed.
In light of these circumstances, the subscriber must take all appropriate measures to protect his data and/or programs, especially from exposure to viruses spread over the internet or unauthorized access to his terminal device system for any purpose. It is recommended to change login information for internet access as soon as the service is subscribed to and regularly update it. Additionally, some harmful content (viruses, unknown applications, etc.) may lead to damaging equipment and data, enabling unauthorized access, or resulting in additional international call charges. Customers are advised to use suitable antivirus programs, read their terms of use, keep them updated, and download applications from known and reliable sources while regularly backing up data. ATM Mobilis also informs subscribers that the safety, health, and confidentiality of information, files, and data, regardless of their nature, exchanged over the internet, cannot be guaranteed on this network. Therefore, customers should refrain from sending messages over the internet that they wish to keep confidential.
    
    7.4 Internet Use by Minors or Vulnerable Individuals: ATM Mobilis does not exercise any control over content. Therefore, parents should monitor their minor children when accessing content on the internet. On the other hand, ATM Mobilis offers its customers the “Parental Control” feature, allowing parents to accompany and protect their children with maximum assistance from unwanted content on the internet.

    7.5 Alert Regarding Data Balance Usage: Automatic updates implemented by terminal devices and/or installed dedicated programs result in significant internet consumption and generate costs that fall on the user without his knowledge. ATM Mobilis recommends reviewing the update settings on the terminal device.

8. Responsibilities: As a network access provider of the GSM/3G/4G type, ATM Mobilis does not exercise any control or monitoring over audio-visual content or any other content transmitted through its network. However, upon notification by a judicial authority, ATM Mobilis reserves the right to suspend or immediately cut off access to its network for the sender and/or recipient of content that is subject to dispute, without prior notice or compensation. The subscriber is informed of the details related to their calls or personal information, as per the applicable legislation, which is stored for one year and can only be accessed in case of a warrant issued by the competent authorities.

9. SIM/USIM Card Lost / Stolen / Damaged
    9.1. SIM/USIM Card Lost / Stolen: In case of loss or stealing of the SIM or prepaid USIM chip card, the subscriber must immediately inform ATM Mobilis to enable the suspension of this card for all incoming and outgoing communications. In this case, the subscriber must present his valid ID card and a copy of the prepaid payment contract.
    • For public or private legal entities, entrepreneurs or individuals working as self-employment, they must provide, in addition to the user’s original and valid ID card and a copy of it, a copy of the prepaid payment contract, a written request on a document bearing the company’s data and stamp.
    • Changing SIM/USIM: For individual: reactivation of the subscriber's line with another SIM/USIM card will only be carried out after the subscriber provides a certificate of loss or theft issued by the competent authorities and a copy of the valid ID card. For legal entities: to reactivate the line by giving another SIM/USIM card to a public or private legal entity, entrepreneur or individual working as self-employment, a certificate of loss or theft issued by the competent authorities, a copy of the valid ID card of the line user or the company representative, and a written request for a new SIM/USIM card bearing the company’s data and stamp are required.
    The responsibility lies with the subscriber who did not follow the above-mentioned procedures for any fraudulent use or violation of public order for his SIM or prepaid USIM chip card.
    
    9.2. SIM/USIM card damage: In case of any SIM/USIM card damage, the subscriber must submit the damaged SIM/USIM card for replacement. For public or private legal entities, entrepreneurs or individuals working as self-employment, they must present the SIM/USIM chip card, in addition to submitting a request for a SIM/USIM card change bearing the company’s data and stamp. ATM Mobilis is not responsible towards the subscriber regarding the effects of theft, loss, or damage to his SIM/USIM card for “prepaid ATM Mobilis” or recharge cards.

10. Warranty: Upon purchasing any terminal device from ATM Mobilis, the latter guarantees the customer against any errors or defects in production. In this regard, the subscriber benefits from a warranty period of 12 months starting from the date of signing the contract. This warranty includes spare parts and after sales service according to the conditions specified by the manufacturer. External damages or damages resulting from the misuse of the purchased products are excluded from the warranty. Accessories such as batteries, chargers, and earphones are also not covered by the warranty from any supplier. Upon identifying a defect, the subscriber must approach the commercial agencies of ATM Mobilis or after-sales service points of authorized suppliers. The warranty covers either repairing the product or, if necessary, replacing it according to the after-sales service procedures set by ATM Mobilis.

11. Termination Procedure: The contract is terminated by operation of law in the event of the withdrawal, cancellation, or expiration of the validity period of the licenses or administrative authorizations issued to ATM Mobilis for the exploitation of the network or any of its components.
    - The subscriber who does not comply with the conditions mentioned in Article 1.1.3 is considered an inactive customer, and the SIM/USIM card will be suspended. However, before any suspension, ATM Mobilis informs the subscriber, through any means of communication, who does not meet his obligations as specified in Article 1.1.3, to remind his of the need to make or receive a voice or video call, send SMS or MMS, contact via the internet, before the expiry of the SIM/USIM card validity period. Otherwise, ATM Mobilis will suspend the SIM/USIM card, and afterward, the customer is not entitled to request the recovery of his previous number under any circumstances, resulting in the termination of the current contract by operation of law.

12. Dispute Settlement Terms and Jurisdiction: Before any dispute related to the services provided by ATM Mobilis, a claim can be submitted either through an ATM. Mobilis’ agency, a point of presence, or a call center. Claims can also be submitted via the official website of ATM Mobilis (www.mobilis.dz) or by regular mail sent to the Directorate General of ATM Mobilis, located in Algiers at “Quartier d'Affaires d'Alger, ilot 05, lots 27, 28 et 29, Bab Ezzouar, Alger”. Depending on the nature of the claim, the subscriber will receive an immediate response or a later response according to the complexity of the request. However, the subscriber will be informed of the response as soon as possible. If the subscriber considers the received response unsatisfactory, he has the right to submit a written appeal to ATM Mobilis at the aforementioned address. If, after reviewing the appeal file, it is found that ATM Mobilis cannot respond to the subscriber’s request, the subscriber will be summoned in writing to seek an amicable solution at the address mentioned above. In case of a dispute and failure to settle it amicably, both parties agree to present their dispute before the competent Algerian judicial authorities, and Algerian law will be applied.

13. Closure of Terminal Devices:
    13.1 The closure period for terminal devices is set at 12 months from the date of contract conclusion.
    13.2 Users have the right to change the SIM card for their locked mobile phones without changing the network.
    13.3 Users can request to deactivate the closure mechanism at any time. For this purpose, they may request the termination of their contract before the expiration of the closure period, subject to payment of a specified fee based on the elapsed period. The user will be notified of this fee according to the specific conditions.

14. After-Sales Service of ATM Mobilis: An after-sales service for the 2G/3G/4G network is provided to subscribers, managing all customer requests related to information, services, and technical assistance associated with “voice” and “data” services on various terminal devices (mobile, smartphone, and USB key), through:
    14.1 Call Centers: ATM Mobilis call centers are established to receive telephone calls, with the capacity continually expanded and adapted according to the workload.
    14.2 Agencies and Points of Presence: All commercial agencies and points of presence of ATM Mobilis, open throughout the national territory, are responsible for taking care of customers. They address their requests and claims concerning “face-to-face” offers and services through sales agents.
    14.3 Website: The “Subscriber Space” is available for ATM Mobilis customers through the official website. This section includes features such as the “FAQs”, “Contact Us” and “Help and Programming”. It will be enriched with additional features, including web assistance, for the benefit of internet users and users of the 2G/3G/4G services.
    14.4 Processing via Mail and Fax: In addition to the access methods mentioned above, customers can submit their requests and claims via fax or mail. These submissions will be received and processed on a case-by-case basis, with responses provided as promptly as possible through telephone communication.

15. Directory and Guidance Service:
    15.1 Subscribers to ATM Mobilis services who refuse to have their names listed in the general directory of subscribers and the telephone guidance service may express their preference in writing when purchasing a SIM card.
    15.2 Customer requests, as mentioned above, do not apply to those not legally authorized to access their information under Algerian law.

16. Review of Contractual Terms: Any modification and/or addition to one or more terms that may arise during the execution of the current contract and its annexes must be the subject of a signed annex after the agreement of both parties.

